# Native projects and dependencies are irrelevant to the web build and
# together contain 70k+ files — well past Vercel's per-deploy file cap.
# Vercel installs its own node_modules server-side from package-lock.json.
node_modules/
ios/
android/
.expo/
dist/
.git/

# Local env files. `.vercelignore` REPLACES `.gitignore` for CLI deploys, so
# without this line the gitignored `.env.local` is uploaded and `expo export`
# reads it during the build — baking local development values (a dev payment
# provider, placeholder keys) into a production bundle. Vercel's own project
# environment variables are the only source of truth for a deploy.
.env
.env*.local

# Build artefacts and scratch space. Neither is part of the web bundle, and
# together they were 25k of the 36k files being uploaded — past Vercel's
# 15k-file limit, which is what forced `--archive=tgz` and turned a deploy
# into a multi-minute upload. `build/` holds native/Xcode output and design
# captures; `.tmp/` is scratch from `npm run db:bundle`.
build/
.tmp/
.vercel/
